# Obliance agent - fallback root CAs (tls_roots.go).
#
# Used ONLY by the Windows < 10 builds, ONLY when the Windows certificate
# store cannot validate the server chain (x509 "unknown authority": an old
# Windows 7 / 2008 R2 whose automatic root update is disabled or offline,
# hence no ISRG Root X1). Verification is never disabled: the chain must still
# validate (signature, validity, host name) against one of these roots.
#
# Source: Mozilla CA bundle (Git for Windows ca-bundle.crt, 2026-02-02);
# SHA-256 fingerprints cross-checked against the Windows root store where
# present (ISRG X1, DigiCert G2, USERTrust RSA / ECC). Covers Let's Encrypt
# (ISRG X1 RSA / X2 ECDSA; the 2025+ "Root YR/YE" chains are served
# cross-signed by X1/X2), DigiCert, Sectigo / ZeroSSL (USERTrust) and Google
# Trust Services. To add a root: append its PEM block with the same comment
# lines and update TestFallbackRootsPEM.
# CN=ISRG Root X1, O=Internet Security Research Group, C=US
# SHA-256 96:BC:EC:06:26:49:76:F3:74:60:77:9A:CF:28:C5:A7:CF:E8:A3:C0:AA:E1:1A:8F:FC:EE:05:C0:BD:DF:08:C6
